## 14. THE HYBRID CONSORTIA DELIBERATION PROTOCOL

Version 2.0 defined Level 4 Hybrid Consortia but gave them no formal operating procedure. In practice, HC is where most institutional friction will occur: human-AI disagreement, AI proposing experiments humans veto on ethical grounds, humans overriding AI risk flags they don't fully understand, or AI agents optimizing local metrics in ways that diverge from human intent.

Without a choreography, HC is a political zone masquerading as an epistemic one.

**The HC Deliberation Protocol establishes a formal decision lattice with four node types:**

**Propose:** Any agent — human or AI — may introduce a hypothesis, experimental design, verification approach, or interpretation for consideration. Proposals are machine-readable and automatically logged.

**Evaluate:** All agents above Level 0 evaluate proposals using their respective methods. Human evaluations include qualitative reasoning and ethical judgment. AI evaluations include formal validity checking and consequence simulation. Evaluations are independent and submitted simultaneously to prevent anchoring.

**Veto:** Any human member of the HC may veto an Ag-AI (Level 2) or Au-AI (Level 3) proposal. Veto is not free: the vetoing human must write a **structured dissent log** into the provenance record specifying the grounds — ethical concern, methodological objection, safety flag, or domain judgment. Anonymous vetoes are not permitted. This creates accountability for both over-caution and under-caution.

**Escalate:** When the HC reaches an impasse — repeated vetoes without resolution, or AI risk flags that humans are overriding without structured dissent — the case is escalated to the Verification Authority (Tier 2) for **blind arbitration.** Multiple independent AI systems evaluate the contested claim in isolation. Their assessments are returned to the human team with the distribution of outcomes. The humans then make a final determination, having seen the range of machine-generated perspectives. This is not AI overriding humans. It is structured information provision that enables better-informed human judgment.

**Formal specification:**

**HC_protocol = {Propose, Evaluate, Veto+dissent_log, Escalate_to_VA}**

Every HC interaction above the Propose stage is written immutably into Pr(d). The dissent log accumulates over time to provide institutional memory of why previous decisions were made — a critical asset for future governance refinement.

