## 17. THE GOVERNANCE ARCHITECTURE

**Tier 1 — The Scientific Council (SC).** Elected researchers, selected through the DCU system, setting institutional weights α, β, γ, δ in V_net; the risk aversion vector λ; equity fraction ε_equity; and stability threshold κ_max. Meets in continuous session with AI-augmented deliberation tools. Updates parameters on a quarterly cycle. All votes publicly recorded.

**Tier 2 — The Verification Authority (VA).** An independent body auditing the ARN, certifying SDL platforms, adjudicating attribution disputes, and conducting blind arbitration in escalated HC deliberations. The VA has no power over hypothesis prioritization. It operates exclusively on verification, attribution, and escalation.

**Tier 3 — The Risk Review Board (RRB).** A specialized standing body with representation from biosecurity, cybersecurity, geopolitics, and ethics. Makes publication channel decisions (Open / Restricted / Sealed). Has veto authority over immediate release. Convened automatically when PERS-Block is triggered or when the cascade stability constraint is threatened.

**Tier 4 — The Public Interface (PI).** A transparent, publicly accessible dashboard showing: the current state of G(t) in accessible language; the hypothesis queue and its prioritization rationale; ARN replication backlogs and success rates; Sealed Discovery sunset timelines without content; equity allocation metrics and their effectiveness; Safety Kernel alert summaries; and DCU leaderboards at the institutional, not individual, level to resist personality cults in science.

