APPENDIX D: FORMAL PROTOCOL SPECIFICATIONS

D.1 Hybrid Consortia Deliberation Protocol — State Machine

The HC protocol is a finite state machine with the following specification:

States: {Idle, Proposing, Evaluating, Deliberating, Escalated, Resolved}
Transitions:

```
Idle → Proposing:  Any agent submits Proposal
Proposing → Evaluating:  Proposal logged, evaluation window opens
Evaluating → Deliberating:  All evaluations received OR timeout
Deliberating → Idle:  Consensus reached, action logged
Deliberating → Proposing:  Counter-proposal generated
Deliberating → Escalated:  Veto without resolution OR impasse detected
Escalated → Resolved:  VA blind arbitration complete
Resolved → Idle:  Determination logged in Pr(d)
```

Evaluation window parameters:

· Standard HC: 72 hours for human evaluation, 6 hours for AI evaluation
· Urgent HC (τ(h) > θ_urgent): 12 hours human, 1 hour AI
· Emergency HC (τ(h) > θ_emergency): 4 hours human, 15 minutes AI

Veto logging requirements:

```
VetoRecord = {
    vetoing_agent: ID,
    vetoed_proposal: ProposalID,
    timestamp: TrustedTimestamp,
    grounds: Enum{Ethical, Methodological, Safety, DomainJudgment},
    detailed_rationale: String(min_length=200_chars),
    suggested_remediation: Optional[Proposal]
}
```

