D.2 Verification Embargo Protocol

Trigger conditions:

· Evidence that an entity has executed unlogged physical synthesis matching a Sealed Discovery
· Evidence obtained through: intelligence sharing, open-source monitoring, whistleblower reports, or AINS instrument network anomaly detection

Protocol execution:

```
1.  VA receives trigger evidence
2.  VA convenes emergency panel (quorum: 7 members, 4 jurisdictions minimum)
3.  Panel evaluates evidence in closed session (72 hours maximum)
4.  If evidence meets "clear and convincing" standard:
5.      Embargo enacted for specified duration (1-5 years, renewable)
6.      Affected entity loses:
7.          - GCC compute access
8.          - SDL network participation
9.          - Formal proof library access
10.         - Open G(t) query access
11.     Embargo registered on AINS public ledger
12.     Affected entity may appeal after 50% of embargo duration
13.     Appeal heard by full RRB with entity representation permitted
```

