E.2 Transitional Dual-Credit Framework

To prevent early-career researcher disenfranchisement during the transition from legacy publishing to AINS, the following framework operates during Phase 0-2:

DCU-to-Impact-Factor Bridge:

· AINS computes a DCU score for each researcher
· An independent Translational Metrics Board (TMB) maps DCU ranges to equivalent legacy metric bands
· Researchers may present both their DCU ledger and their TMB-equivalency certificate to hiring, promotion, and funding committees
· The TMB dissolves at the end of Phase 2, by which point DCUs should have achieved sufficient institutional recognition

Non-Participant Integration:

· Publications from non-AINS institutions are ingested into G(t) as External Provisional nodes
· They carry a flag: "This node has not been independently replicated by AINS. Confidence estimates are based on legacy peer review alone."
· ARN triages External Provisional nodes for replication based on their potential impact on G(t), not their journal of origin
· Authors may opt into full AINS provenance logging for their next work without leaving their home institution

