F.1 G(t) Graph Schema

Node types:

· DISCOVERY: A scientific claim (theorem, experimental result, model)
· DATASET: A collection of data with provenance
· METHOD: A protocol, algorithm, or experimental technique
· AGENT: A human or AI contributor
· INSTITUTION: An organization housing agents or infrastructure
· INSTRUMENT: A physical or computational apparatus

Edge types:

· SUPPORTS: Node A provides evidence for Node B (weight: confidence increment)
· CONTRADICTS: Node A provides evidence against Node B (weight: confidence decrement)
· DEPENDS_ON: Node B's validity requires Node A's validity
· DERIVED_FROM: Node B was algorithmically generated from Node A
· REPLICATES: Node B is an independent replication attempt of Node A
