F.3 Global Compute Commons — Technical Architecture

Resource pooling model:
Contributions from member states and institutions are pooled into a virtualized compute grid with the following allocation classes:

· Class A (Subsidized): For institutions with M(a) < M_global. Cost: 10% of market rate. Funded by member state contributions.
· Class B (Standard): For institutions with M(a) ≥ M_global but below top quartile. Cost: market rate.
· Class C (Premium): For institutions in top quartile. Cost: 120% of market rate, with surplus funding Class A subsidies.
· Class E (Equity Allocation): Reserved for ε_equity-mandated projects from underrepresented institutions. Cost: zero.

Oversight:
GCC allocation is auditable in real time through the Public Interface dashboard. Any member state contributing resources may verify that its contributions are being allocated according to the published formula. Allocation disputes are adjudicated by the VA.

